WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.735
Now to a big policy pivot

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.702
from Florida Governor Ron

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.771
DeSantis that reflects a giant change

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.239
in Republican priorities.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.907
DeSantis now says backing

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.510
Ukraine is not not a vital U.S.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.112
interest. Look at this.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.014
While the United States has many vital

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.181
national interests

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:15.949
becoming further

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:18.184
entangled in a territorial dispute

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.953
between Ukraine and Russia, it's

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:20.854
not one of them.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.455
His answer, part of a questionnaire.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.256
The Fox host Tucker

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.758
Carlson sent to Republican

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.126
presidential hopefuls

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.528
or great reporters are back at the table.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.398
Ron DeSantis now says it is not a vital

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.632
US interest, and he calls it

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.768
a territorial dispute.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.702
Ron DeSantis,

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.203
as a member of the House

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.905
in the Obama administration,

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:39.739
we in the Congress

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.940
have been urging the president,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.909
I've been to provide arms to Ukraine.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.210
They want to fight their good fight.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:44.978
They're not asking us

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.046
to fight it for them.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:46.713
And the president

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.081
has steadfastly refused.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.783
And I think that's a mistake.

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.784
So a flip flop.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.653
Why the Tucker tail is wagging the dog.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.187
That's why.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.623
I mean, look at the forum

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:57.524
through which he wanted

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.825
to give this information

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.528
from a host on Fox News

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:05.365
who has been railing against the U.S.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.966
involvement in Ukraine,

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.468
has been supporting

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.303
autocrats who are

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.038
in and around the region.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.507
And this is a person

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.842
who has a large audience

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.777
within the Republican electorate.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:18.778
And so that's why

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.513
you see a flip flop there.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.181
What's interesting

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.082
is, as

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.249
you were talking about that,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.185
Nikki Haley, former U.S.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.686
ambassador to the U.N.,

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.955
came out with her answers to that.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:29.756
I mean, by the way.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.291
Can we just talk about the fact that

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.392
it is Tucker Carlson

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.027
who is sending questionnaires

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.863
to these candidates that says everything,

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.331
but she's stuck,

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.833
stuck to the more traditional

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.633
Republican line,

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.235
which is, yes, it is important

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.004
to us national interest to stay and help

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.239
the Ukrainians.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.207
And so let's go through

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.108
some of the different answers

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:48.808
which tell you

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:49.442
we are no longer

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.310
living in Ronald Reagan's

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:50.910
Republican Party.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.811
There are still people like

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.546
Nikki Haley who voiced that view.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.547
But it's increasingly,

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.049
I would say, a minority are,

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.151
you know, Donald Trump No.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.586
The question is, is opposing Russia

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.019
and Ukraine

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.287
a vital American national

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:01.988
strategic interest?

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.022
Donald Trump says no,

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:03.990
but it is for Europe,

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.458
but not for the United States.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.726
Mike Pence disagrees.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:07.827
When the United States supports

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.262
Ukraine in their fight against Putin.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.697
We follow the Reagan doctrine.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:11.664
DeSantis again.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.398
He's with Trump

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.299
more or less becoming

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.000
further entangled

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.435
in a territorial dispute

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.369
between Ukraine and Russia.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.370
Is not one of them.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.705
Nikki Haley, as you know, says, yes,

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.472
the Russian government

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.673
is a powerful dictatorship

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.075
that makes no secret of its hatred

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:22.809
of America.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.677
And fellow South Carolinian Tim Scott.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.912
Degrading the Russian military

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.081
is in our vital national interest.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.582
Even the way the question is framed

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.985
in the idea that this is it.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.353
Ron DeSantis wants to makes it

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.854
about Russia and Ukraine.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.356
Putin and Zelensky

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.924
as opposed to an attack

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.926
on a huge democracy in Europe.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.129
Access to Ukrainian, the the breadbasket,

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:43.997
if you will, of Europe.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:44.531
All that

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:46.232
the economic and agricultural power

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:46.900
that would give him.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.568
And then what about Moldova?

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.570
What about the natal countries,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.471
the Eastern European countries

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.906
that joined native Natal?

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.474
Well,
I think the answer from

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.175
a lot of the Republican

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.576
presidential Kansas Republican

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.344
primary voters would be.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.846
So what about Moldova? Right.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:00.413
This is a party

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.848
that just doesn't really care

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.550
about that stuff in the same way,

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.951
or at least that's what it looks like

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.752
on the surface. Right now.

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.620
And I think one of the big questions

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.756
about this race, right for years now,

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.124
the loudest voices

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:13.126
in the Republican Party have been saying

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.427
what we hear from Donald Trump. Right?

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.361
That's not our problem.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.362
That's Europe's problem.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.964
It's a territorial dispute

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.632
that doesn't concern us.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.066
You know,

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.335
I am old enough to remember

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.503
when this was a really solidly

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.337
hawkish party

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.205
and when an underdog

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.739
presidential candidate

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:27.974
and John McCain

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:28.741
back in

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.610
2008, sort of rose from the dead

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.679
as a candidate on the strength of his,

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.147
you know, sort of hawkish

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.215
policy credentials.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.350
And I do wonder how much there is

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.985
some of that vestigial DNA

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:39.786
still in the party

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:40.286
that it

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.487
as you ask the question is,

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.488
do you want to sort of

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.856
go to the wall for Ukraine?

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.390
A lot of people

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.391
might shy away from that,

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.459
but do you support

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.194
a strong and assertive America?

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:50.296
Do you support a world that is,

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.631
you know,
led by the United States

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.632
and not sort of shared

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.500
by a couple of different superpowers?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.735
I do think those instincts

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:56.703
are still there.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.537
And the question is,

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:58.538
is there someone in the race

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.072
who can play?

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.306
He's old enough to remember.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.408
I mean, it wasn't that long ago.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.410
the issue at the Sanders tries

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:04.711
to make

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.312
this point, Republicans are trying to say

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.580
stand up to China

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.948
and sort of never mind Europe,

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.917
never mind Putin, never mind Russia.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.185
The question is, can you make that?

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.253
Can you sell that argument

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.787
or will somebody like McCain

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:15.154
stand up and say

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.422
it's a lot more complicated than that.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.890
And everything you do against Russia

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.259
and Ukraine has an impact

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.460
on the China conversation.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.595
But for that person to break through,

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.162
for a Haley

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:23.963
to break through or Pence

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.531
to break through or somebody else,

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.866
they're walking into the heavy breeze

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.601
right now.
This is from our brand new poll.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:29.335
Is it important

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.570
that the Republican nominee believes

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:30.903
the U.S.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.405
should not be involved

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.373
in Russia, Ukraine?

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:35.141
36% more than a third of Republicans

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.075
say it's essential.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.177
44% say it's important to them.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:38.911
So add that up.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.281
80% of Republican voters

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.815
or potential Republican voters

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:43.349
don't think it's

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:44.817
it's not

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.252
important to them, essentially,

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.453
that the Republicans agree

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:48.721
with President Biden on this.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.622
And you do see

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.790
dampening support

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.825
among Republicans on this issue.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.294
But that that is not

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:54.961
the same as what you're

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.329
seeing in Congress with in Congress.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:57.764
This is still where you're describing

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:59.132
it is a minority viewpoint.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.433
I've talked to almost

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.434
a dozen lawmakers

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.235
recently about this

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.436
on both sides of the aisle.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.804
And they still feel strongly

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.706
about support for Ukraine.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:09.509
Now, there is that Ukraine fatigue group

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.110
that Matt Gates is leading.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.679
There's roughly a dozen lawmakers

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:13.346
in that in the House

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.414
that does not want to provide

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:15.448
further support to Ukraine.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:16.082
But again,

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.617
there's there's only 11 people

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.285
who've signed on to that resolution.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.987
As for this questionnaire,

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.121
Asa Hutchinson, the former

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.089
governor of Arkansas,

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.091
was one of those who did not answer it.

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:25.925
But in an interview

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.660
over the weekend with USA Today,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.962
he linked China and Ukraine together

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:30.430
and said

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.597
he sees this as important

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.966
to deterring China from invading Taiwan.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.401
One of my favorite subplots

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.236
is the Florida Republican debate.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.538
You have Trump and DeSantis

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:39.405
essentially on the same page

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:40.073
when it comes to Ukraine.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:40.673
Marco Rubio,

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.908
who's not running this time

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:42.809
said on YouTube today

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.377
there is a national security interest

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:45.211
in Ukraine.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.346
And he said DeSantis, quote,

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:47.580
doesn't deal with foreign policy

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.681
every day as governor.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.184
So we'll poke a little poke there.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:52.051
We're just getting started

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:52.852
in the Republican race.

